      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Appointment Booking\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow exposes webhook endpoints for an appointment-booking assistant. The main webhook inspects the incoming request to decide whether to check Cal.com availability, create a booking, or return an unknown-tool response. It then calls the relevant Cal.com API endpoint and responds to the original webhook with available slots, booking success, or booking error details; a separate small webhook path returns a direct response for a secondary endpoint.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the webhook URLs in n8n and point the calling application or AI tool to the production webhook endpoint for the main appointment flow.\n- Add the required Cal.com API authentication to the HTTP Request nodes, including the API key or bearer token expected by the Cal.com v2 API.\n- Review the IF node conditions so they match the exact request fields used to indicate slot lookup versus appointment booking.\n- Confirm the Cal.com event type, attendee, date/time, timezone, and other booking payload fields in the slot-check and booking HTTP requests.\n- Test each path: available-slot lookup, successful booking, booking failure, unknown-tool fallback, and the secondary webhook endpoint.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can adapt the IF conditions for different tool names or request schemas, change the Cal.com endpoints or event types, and modify the webhook responses to match the format expected by your chatbot or frontend."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "34ce870e-b513-43b5-a49f-e2ac15a7583e",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
